    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your companion is a pungent herd beast popular among hobgoblins as a mount or pack animal.</p><p><strong>Size</strong> Medium</p><p><strong>Melee</strong> <span class=\"pf2-icon\">1</span> horn, Damage 1d8 piercing</p><p><strong>Melee</strong> <span class=\"pf2-icon\">1</span> hoof (agile), Damage 1d6 bludgeoning</p><p><strong>Str</strong> +3, <strong>Con</strong> +2, <strong>Dex</strong> +2, <strong>Int</strong> –4, <strong>Wis</strong> +1, <strong>Cha</strong> +0</p><p><strong>Hit Points</strong> 6</p><p><strong>Skill</strong> Intimidation</p><p><strong>Speed</strong> 30 feet</p><p><strong>Special</strong> mount</p><p><strong>Support Benefit</strong> Your yzobu releases a foul odor. Until the start of your next turn, if you hit and deal damage to a creature within your yzobu's reach, the creature is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 1}. This sickened condition ends automatically after 1 round, without the creature needing to retch.</p><p><strong>Advanced Maneuver</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e-animal-companions.AC-Advanced-Maneuvers.Item.sRFMyNz46TAxRUy3]{Bucking Trample}</p>",
